BND-18: clear the averages of periods that fall before REPORT_START

With [REPORT] AVERAGES YES, output_saveResults() returned for report times
before REPORT_START without saving, and so without the call to
output_initAvgResults() that output_saveAvgResults() makes. The first saved
period then averaged every routing step since START. Re-initialize the
averages when a period is skipped.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-18_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/output.c b/src/legacy/engine/output.c
index f57370e..9d162a9 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/output.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/output.c
@@ -478,7 +478,13 @@ void output_saveResults(double reportTime)
     REAL8 date;
 
     // --- initialize system-wide results
-    if ( reportDate < ReportStart ) return;
+    if ( reportDate < ReportStart )
+    {
+        // --- periods before ReportStart are not saved, so start the
+        //     averages of the first saved period afresh
+        if ( RptFlags.averages ) output_initAvgResults();
+        return;
+    }
     for (i=0; i<MAX_SYS_RESULTS; i++) SysResults[i] = 0.0f;
 
     // --- save date corresponding to this elapsed reporting time
